id: pm-todos-oqrt
title: Preview and materialize stable recurring todo occurrences
description: "Explicit todo.txt recurrence adaptation with stable series and occurrence identities, original due semantics, SDK-owned mutation and retry safety. Overlap recheck: core scheduling stores deadlines, reminders and event recurrence; core defect recurrence reopens work for governance; pm-gantt-chart forecasts work. No existing todo occurrence adapter or tracker item was found. This feature interprets source syntax and prevents duplicate occurrences; it is not a background scheduler or reminder service."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: recurrence,sdk,todotxt
created_at: "2026-10-26T02:22:01.754Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T04:00:24.879Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Repeated weekly completion creates at most one next occurrence; timezone and invalid date cases refuse with exact policy; disabled recurrence preserves source text; typed SDK and CLI previews with compact TOON/JSON and remedies; non-git real SDK, seeded replay/state and concurrency regressions; public tracker read-only validation and npm/Bun CI release gate evidence"
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T02:22:22.317Z",codex-agent,"Overlap verified against the pinned SDK, core scheduling and sibling pm-gantt-chart: source rec tokens are only preserved today. Plan: explicit date-only todo.txt weekly dialect, preview-first stable identities, SDK item locks/import commits and history revisions, no background work. Test replays, foreign identities, custom status roles, invalid calendars and concurrent apply on a plain tracker."
  "2026-10-26T02:34:50.199Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses native SDK creation for atomic stable ids and mutateItem for source locking with no-op history suppression. Each apply requires the preview history record hash and rederives from the locked source. No frozen journal or background scheduler is added. Identity metadata is retained in existing todos_kv fields so JSONL and todo.txt fidelity exports keep it. Native parent/dependency relationships and original source documents are preserved; successors intentionally copy title, priority, tags and source recurrence only. Interleaving probes cover all six observable apply boundaries, including foreign creation and interruption after publication; two independent host processes create exactly one successor."
  "2026-10-26T02:45:49.771Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public corpus validation: 99 committed items; 93 done, 4 active, 1 canceled, 1 other. No retained todo.txt sources or recurrence tokens, so no natural positive recurrence candidate. Disabled: 99 no-ops. Enabled: 93 invalid_source and 6 not_done refusals; maximum JSON receipt 228 bytes; all 212 file/directory entries byte-identical; no git executable and no synthetic corpus rows. This also found 65 valid legacy history tips without record hashes; revision fallback hashes the SDK-read verified full chain instead of rewriting history or using item content alone."
  "2026-10-26T02:49:13.215Z",codex-agent,"Seed 0x72656375 completed 500 random sequences: 813 native/legacy imports, 419 syncs, 1232 exports followed by reimport, 722 older-input replays and 633 CRLF variants. All comparisons read persisted native state through SDK document readers against a separate native-SDK reference tracker; relationship provenance and body survived, and the source retained at most one successor. Behavioral revert proof: replacing only applyTodoOccurrence with the pre-feature disabled no-op made the weekly regression fail (expected created, actual disabled; exit 1); source restored byte-identically. Final linked targeted rerun follows after refusal/schema additions."
  "2026-10-26T02:57:41.420Z",codex-agent,"Linked validation passed: 6 feature tests including the 500-sequence SDK/reference model; after the final stable-key refinement, all 6 focused non-model regressions passed again through pm test. Replaying old JSONL through native and legacy importers after inherited series metadata is removed cannot create a second successor. Reverting only the predecessor-only identity tuple to a series-dependent tuple makes that regression fail (exit 1); source restored byte-identically. Final typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. No separate lint script is configured. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun release gates will be the PR CI evidence; local full gates were intentionally not run on the shared host. Remaining scope limits: floating weekly dates only; public corpus has no natural positive source; imported occurrence provenance is not adopted."
  "2026-10-26T03:23:21.048Z",codex-agent,"Review #156 blocked computed unchanged receipts: changing a completed source rule could report an intended next date while leaving the successor at its old date. Reusing this feature item to close the class: SDK read-back schedule receipts, stored-versus-intended reschedule plans, successor revision CAS under its native lock, preservation/refusal of manual schedule or lifecycle edits, and a second 500-sequence source/successor operation model plus behavioral revert proof."
  "2026-10-26T03:43:52.210Z",codex-agent,"Implemented one SDK read-back builder for existing and post-create/reschedule receipts; intended schedules are separate from stored facts. Reschedule compares the exact previewed target revision under its native lock, with the source lease retained through final read-back. SDK replay reconstructs the last package-written deadline/rule/original due/anchor/status and retained source tokens; manual due, token or lifecycle edits refuse as foreign_schedule. Deleted successors refuse as target_deleted; no replay resurrection. Fixed review case and all seven reschedule interleaving boundaries pass, including after-publication and final-release peer edits; packed CLI target-revision flag also passes."
  "2026-10-26T03:51:33.958Z",codex-agent,"New stored-schedule model passed 500 sequences (250 each for seeds 0x51ceda7a and 0x20261026): 7524 SDK/model state-checked steps, 524 reschedules, 145 unchanged outcomes, 211 manual-edit refusals and 399 replays. It covers source interval/unit/due/completion/reopen/deletion and successor manual due/completion/deletion/status plus preview/apply/replay. Revert proof: restoring the computed existing-target receipt path in storedReceipt only makes this model fail at seed 0x51ceda7a sequence 0 bootstrap preview (expected reschedule, actual unchanged; exit 1). Original source restored byte-identically. Final focused linked tests and CI follow; finished prior corpus validation is retained rather than repeated."
  "2026-10-26T04:00:23.384Z",codex-agent,"Final focused linked run: 9 passed, 0 failed (including fixed review case, all reschedule boundaries, real packed CLI, and independent retained-token hand edits). Source/type checks and docstring lint pass. Host TOON formatting omits null properties, so absent successor previews use targetExists=false rather than an ambiguous null stored marker; materialized receipts use targetExists=true and SDK-read facts. The strengthened model also checks retained source/target due and rule tokens and native source/target revision coordinates. Review follow-up is ready for the unchanged npm/Bun CI release gates."
